AWS EC2 Infrastructure Setup and Deployment

Step-by-Step Implementation

step 1: Logged into the AWS account.
    Selected the Sydney region (ap-southeast-2).
    Configured AWS CLI authentication using aws login.
    Verified AWS account credentials.
    Command used: aws sts get-caller-identity

Step 2: EC2 Instance Launch
    Navigated to the EC2 service in the AWS Management Console.
    Launched an EC2 virtual machine.
    Selected Ubuntu as the operating system.
    Selected the t3.micro instance type.
    Configured the required key pair for SSH authentication.
    Configured the network and security group.
    Successfully launched the instance.

The instance state was verified as Running, with all three status checks passing.

Step 3: Security Group Configuration
    Configured inbound security group rules to allow HTTP and SSH traffic.
    Type    Protocol    Port          Source                Purpose
    HTTP     TCP         80          0.0.0.0/0             Public web access
    SSH      TCP         22      My-IP (1.38.148.197/32)   Secure terminal access
    The SSH rule was updated to allow connections from the current public IP address.

Step 4: SSH Connection to EC2
    Established a remote SSH connection from the local Ubuntu terminal (WSL) to the EC2 instance.
    First, configured the private key permissions: chmod 400 ~/.ssh/"EC2 Instance Key.pem"
    Connected to the EC2 instance using: ssh -i ~/.ssh/"EC2 Instance Key.pem" ubuntu@32.236.18.60
    Successfully established SSH connectivity and accessed the Ubuntu server terminal.
    The connection was also verified using: nc -zv 32.236.18.60 22

Step 5: Nginx Web Server Configuration
Configured the Nginx web server on the Ubuntu EC2 instance.
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install nginx
    sudo systemctl start nginx
    sudo systemctl enable nginx
    sudo systemctl status nginx
    Verified web server accessibility using the instance's public IPv4 address:
    http://32.236.18.60
    The Nginx welcome page was successfully accessible through a web browser, confirming that HTTP traffic was reaching the instance.

Step 6: AMI Creation and Backup
    Created an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) from the running EC2 instance using the AWS Management Console.
    Procedure:
    Navigated to EC2 → Instances.
    Selected the target EC2 instance.
    Opened Actions → Image and templates.
    Selected Create image.
    Provided the AMI name: Snapbox-AMI-Backup.
    Submitted the image creation request.
    Verified the AMI under EC2 → Images → AMIs.
    AMI creation confirmation and AMI status showing Available.











